
class:: ViewCentral
summary:: The view component for model-view window classes that centre a view within a variable size window, maintaining a fixed view size.
categories:: gui>views
related:: Classes/ViewCentralModel, Classes/UserView, Classes/View, Classes/Window

description::
ViewCentral is the view component in a model-view architecture for window management. It handles the visual representation of state maintained by a ViewCentralModel instance. The class maintains a fixed view size, however view margins and window size can be altered. These classes can be used to fullscreen a window while keeping a view centered.

note::
User interaction is not intended directly with ViewCentral methods. With the exception of the the four methods below, all operations are intended for the model. See link::Classes/ViewCentralModel::.
::

classmethods::

method:: new
Creates a new ViewCentral instance with the given window and model.

argument:: win
A Window instance. If nil, a new Window will be created.

argument:: model
A ViewCentralModel instance.


instancemethods::

private:: init, applyMarginCol, applyViewCol, applyWinCol, applyWinName, applyMargins, applyWinSize, applyWinPos, applyRemove, applyFullScreen, applyFront, applyEndFullScreen, applyClose, registerKeyDownAction, registerWinAction, getScreenHeight, makeLayout, update

method:: win
Returns the managed Window instance.

method:: view
Returns the content view (either a UserView or View) where custom drawing can be performed.

method:: marginView
Returns the containing View with margins.

method:: model
Returns the ViewCentralModel that controls this view.


examples::

code::
// Make a model, pass into the view
m = ViewCentralModel.new([1080, 720]);
v = ViewCentral.new(model: m);

// Return the model via the view if needed
v.model

// Access gui elements directly
v.win
v.view
v.marginView

// Methods should be performed from the model
m.front;
m.margins_(50);
m.viewCol_(Color.blue);
m.marginCol_(Color.rand);

// Close the window
m.close;
::